00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.180
Happy Death Day 2U opens with Ryan waking
up in his car filled with Hot Pocket wrappers

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:50.690
and walking down the street to go back to
the dorm on the morning of Tuesday the 19th.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.210
This is just a few minutes before the final
scene of the first movie, where Ryan does

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.620
make a reference to having to sleep in the
car.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.620
“She’s back?”

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.620
“Out.”

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.460
“I’m not sleeping in my car again, it
smells like hot pockets and feet.”

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.890
When Ryan gets into the dorm building, he
crosses through a student blowing a horn at

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:06.890
one of the dorm rooms.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.821
This is the first time we’re seeing something
that is only heard in the first movie, every

00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:15.899
time tree wakes up after the loop resets her
to Monday the 18th, this can be heard in the

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:16.899
distance.

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:18.159
“Shut up!”

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:19.659
“Shut up!”

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:21.170
“Shut up!”

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.670
“Shut up!”

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.179
“Oh hey!”

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:25.689
“Shut up!”

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:28.360
What is this, an early Smosh video?

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.120
“SHUT UP!”

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.679
So after getting kicked out of his room, Ryan
goes to the science building to check on his

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:40.630
invention, the Sisius Quantum Cooling Reactor,
nicknamed the Sissy for short.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.369
Here, we learn that the machine has been eating
up a ton of power to operate, which is the

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:47.040
reason for all the power outages seen in the
first movie.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.480
“Our tuition dollars at work.”

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.340
I don’t know why this machine would affect
the power in other buildings, because that’s

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.619
not really how electricity works, but maybe
it has more to do with the machine’s interdimensional

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.030
effects and less to do with power consumption.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.740
There are a couple of fun set dec things I
noticed in the lab, like a little figurine

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.920
of Nicola Tesla, the guy who basically invented
the alternating current electricity system

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.920
we use today.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.920
There are also some magazines on the table
called Zombie Power Magazine.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.112
This director of the Happy Death Day films,
Christopher Landon also made a zombie movie

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.540
called Scouts Guide To The Zombie Apocalypse.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.980
“Boom.”

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.260
After the school’s Dean tells Ryan they’ll
have to confiscate the machine, he wanders

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.510
around the science building trying to find
his fellow nerds, where he is killed by a

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:38.170
masked Babyface killer, causing his day to
reset to the beginning of Tuesday the 19th,

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.019
so he wakes up in his car, where we can see
his license plate reads “meco” which might

00:02:42.019 --> 00:02:44.750
have something to do with his mechanical engineering
skills.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.519
Ryan gets back to the dorm room and explains
what just happened.

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:51.319
He tells Tree and Carter that he feels like
he’s going through Deja Vu, which is exactly

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:55.459
what Tree said when she first experienced
the time loop in the first film.

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:58.930
“I’m totally having Deja Vu right now.”

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.150
“Oh, I have it all the time.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.200
It’s supposed to mean, like, someone’s
thinking about you while they’re masturbating.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.680
I have it at least five times a day.”

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.719
*sigh* Do you want to tell her or should I?

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:11.250
So they end up going after this new killer
with a baseball bat.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.960
I’m sure the actress Jessica Rothe, who
plays Tree, appreciated having the bat in

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.120
her hands this time.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.680
“I also really like the baseball bat one,
though that one, I did not like shooting,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.840
but no, all of the deaths were really fun.”

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.340
“Why not?”

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.580
“Because, they hit me in the head with a
baseball bat…

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.140
Not a real one!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:29.660
Not a real one.”

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.200
Unfortunately for her, the killer gets away
this time, so they head over to place that

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.280
Carter believes they’ll be safest from the
Baby mask killer…

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.580
The… basketball game… where literally
everybody has a baby mask.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:44.660
The fans of this team really got clever with
their signs, nicknaming their stadium “the

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.170
cradle”, and coming up with slogans such
as “babies gonna deliver,” which is funny

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.731
because usually it’s the doctor who delivers
the baby, but at the end of this movie, its

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:55.199
the babies, delivering a big blow to the doctor,
Dr. Butler.

00:03:55.199 --> 00:03:59.359
Tree also runs into Tim who she gives a thumbs
up when she notices him sitting next to this

00:03:59.359 --> 00:04:00.359
guy in the stands.

00:04:00.359 --> 00:04:04.459
This is a reference to her accidental discovery
that Tim is gay when trying investigate who

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:06.310
her killer is in the first movie.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:10.090
But after the basketball game lets out, Babyface
comes after Ryan with a knife and ends up

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.330
chasing him into the storage area of the Bayfield
University merch store, where Tree knocks

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.769
out the killer with a basketball trophy.

00:04:15.769 --> 00:04:17.419
“I had a little practice.”

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.680
“Well who is it?”

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.820
“Only one way to find out.”

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.540
Huh!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.620
It’s old man Witherspoon from the graveyard!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.840
And he would have gotten away-- oh no nevermind
it’s another Ryan.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.340
So they go back to the lab again...

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.130
“Back to the lab again.”

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.930
...to try to send doppel Ryan back to his
own dimension, but inadvertently end up sending

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:46.500
Tree to another dimension, which I’ll be
calling Dimension B, only in this dimension

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.870
she’s still stuck in Monday the 18th, and
she’s understandably furious at Ryan for

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:51.910
sending her back.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.030
This causes Carter to ask them if they know
each other.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:58.100
Ryan says no, because this version of Ryan
has never met Tree, and Tree says yes, because

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.900
she doesn’t realize this is actually Dimension
B Ryan.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.810
This is an inverse of something that happened
at the sorority lunch in Happy Death Day.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.320
“Wait, you two know each other?”

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.040
“Yeah--”
“No.”

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.180
“We had a class together last year.”

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.710
As the day goes on Tree notices that this
dimension has many differences from her dimension.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.110
Carter and Lori know each other, and by the
way, Lori is not evil now, Danielle and Carter

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.050
are dating because Danielle is seemingly nice
in this dimension.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:29.180
For example, she recommends doing the Special
Needs Art Fair charity and she’s actually

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.830
excited about it in Dimension B, whereas in
Dimension A…

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:38.530
“I can say right now, there’s no way we’re
doing the special needs art fair again.”

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:41.870
There are still fundamental similarities between
the two dimensions though.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:45.669
The power goes out at the same time, Lori
still covers a double shift for Jen at the

00:05:45.669 --> 00:05:46.669
hospital,

00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:47.669
“Doing a double for Jen.

00:05:47.669 --> 00:05:48.669
She has the flu.”

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:52.720
And Tree still has a birthday lunch with her
father at the same time, only in this dimension

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.590
her mother is alive as well and she also attends.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:58.980
The birthday cake that her dad brings out
looks identical to the cake that we see in

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.539
the video on Tree’s phone when she’s looking
back at the memories of her shared birthday

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:03.960
with her mom in the first one.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.970
“Back to the lab again.”

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.539
Tree explains the situation to the nerds,
and Carter compares it to the events of Back

00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:10.599
To The Future Part 2.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:15.020
I guess Tree realllly makes an effort to stay
away from movies, because just like at the

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.940
end of Happy Death Day, Tree has no idea what
he’s talking about.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:21.360
“You now what your little scenario reminds
me of?”

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.040
“What?

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:22.540
What’s that?”

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:23.880
“Groundhog Day.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.120
The movie Groundhog day.”

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:26.760
"I don't know."

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:27.740
“With Bill Murray?”

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.820
“Who’s Bill Murray?”

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.760
Tree realizes one thing that doesn’t add
up in Universe B.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.740
If Carter and Danielle are a couple, then
why does Carter take home Tree?

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.220
Why does she wake up in the dorm room in the
first place?

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:42.080
He tells her that he slept on Ryan’s bed
and he only took her home because he was afraid

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.710
she was going to choke on her own vomit like
Janis Joplin.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:49.229
This is the same line Universe A Carter uses
in the first movie when accused of taking

00:06:49.229 --> 00:06:50.669
advantage of Tree.

00:06:50.669 --> 00:06:55.371
“No, you’re wasted last night, and I was
afraid you were gonna fall or choke on your

00:06:55.371 --> 00:06:57.020
own vomit, like Janis Joplin.”

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.090
So they try running the Sissy machine again,
but it doesn’t work because the nerds don’t

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.350
have the right algorithms.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:06.289
The rattle caused by the machine actually
knocks the clock off the wall, indicating

00:07:06.289 --> 00:07:07.470
progress has been halted.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:11.180
Basically, there’s no way for them to test
all the algorithms in one day, and when the

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.389
day resets, they won’t know which ones have
already been tested.

00:07:14.389 --> 00:07:16.370
That leaves them with only one option.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.470
Tree must memorize each equation, and use
her Reading Steiner ability, or her ability

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:24.650
to carry her memories whenever time is reset,
to let them know which algorithms have already

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:25.650
been tested.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:30.330
That leads us to a suicide montage filled
with outdated memes like Nyan Cat, drinking

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.330
bleach and even FML.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:35.830
A couple of Tree’s self kills contained
some fun references, like the poster on the

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.280
skydiving plane that says “like a leaf.”

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.280
You know.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.680
Because her name is Tree.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.140
And when she throws herself into the woodchipper,
it says “tree removal service on the side

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.140
of it.”

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.000
You know.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:47.600
Because her name is Tree.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.200
I love to think about what happens in all
of these dimensions that Tree dies in.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:55.740
Just think about it, in one of these universes,
there is a reality where Carter and his girlfriend

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:00.280
Danielle are just sitting outside, and all
the sudden Danielle’s half naked best friend

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.300
falls out of the sky and splats on the sidewalk
in front of them.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.830
And they have to deal with that for the rest
on their lives and they never know why.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:10.370
But also during Tree’s many deaths, she
discovers that Lori actually seems to be the

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:13.860
victim in this world, so she spends some of
her time trying to figure out who the killer

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:17.009
is, because, remember, in this one, Lori isn’t
evil.

00:08:17.009 --> 00:08:20.250
During one of the suicides, Tree jumps from
the clock tower and there’s a cool transition

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.909
to her landing in Carters bed to start the
loop over again, it was very similar to my

00:08:23.909 --> 00:08:25.760
favorite death from the first movie.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.880
Eventually, they figure out the correct equation,
and Ryan tells Tree she can choose between

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:40.950
closing the loop and staying in Dimension
B or closing the loop behind her as she goes

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:44.779
back to Dimension A. So she has the decision
to make between her mother and Carter.

00:08:44.779 --> 00:08:45.779
Past, or future.

00:08:45.779 --> 00:08:49.280
And there’s one thing you might have missed
that I think is the key to her making that

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.280
decision.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.190
When she has the heart to heart talk with
her mother at the motel room, she asks her

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:57.410
Mom, what would you do if you had to choose
between Dad and someone else you really cared

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.410
about?

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.490
Her mom says she’d probably choose Tree’s
father, because without him, she never would

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:02.490
have had Tree.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:06.310
I’ll try to refrain from any jokes about
him having “the seed for Tree”, but I

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:10.269
think this is what makes Tree’s decision
to go back to her own dimension make sense.

00:09:10.269 --> 00:09:14.200
She’s not just choosing Carter over her
mom, she’s choosing all the possible future

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.150
memories that she and Carter might share.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.209
Let’s not forget this line from the first
movie.

00:09:18.209 --> 00:09:19.209
“His name’s Carter.

00:09:19.209 --> 00:09:24.320
No, we did not have sex, but if I finally
make it through this day somehow, I’m gonna

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.370
have his babies.”

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:29.280
So in order to stop them from closing the
time-loop and to reset the day all in one

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:34.240
go, she crashes her car into the power distribution
box thing, and decides to give it one more

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.240
go.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.750
She says goodbye to everyone from Dimension
B, where she learns that Danielle was actually

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:42.860
cheating on Carter with Nick, who if you don’t
remember, was Danielle’s crush in the first

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.880
one who Tree made out with at a party.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.980
“It’s fine, you can make it up to me later.”

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.380
“What?”

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.380
“Don’t ‘what’ me!”

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.480
“You know exactly what you’re doing Tree.”

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.870
If we can pause for one second for my personal
opinion even though I’m not supposed to

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.870
have one…

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.690
One thing that kind of bothered me, was that
Tree never tells Carter B that his girlfriend

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:06.690
is unfaithful.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:10.300
She helps out Lori, she gives advice to everyone
else, but she kind of leaves him hanging.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.529
“Back to the lab again.”

00:10:12.529 --> 00:10:16.180
So they get everything figured out, and just
as they’re about to send Tree back home,

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.180
the dean bursts in and takes away their time-travel
machine.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.899
There are some issues with that, but I’ll
come back to it later.

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:24.930
So the gang needs to come up with a plan to
steal the machine back, they use Danielle,

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:29.620
who is an aspiring actress in this universe,
to distract the Dean, while they carry out

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:30.620
their plan.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:34.880
Meanwhile, Tree has one more errand to run
in Universe B. She runs back to the med building

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:38.900
to save Lori from the killer, who she has
figured out is Dr. Butler, but there’s one

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:43.000
thing she didn’t guess -- his wife is also
one of the baby masked killers.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.740
In Happy Death Day, Dr. Butler goes behind
his wife’s back to sleep with Tree, but

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:50.760
in the new universe, it’s Lori, which is
why the only time Tree was targeted in Universe

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.620
B was when she tried to protect Lori.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:56.410
Also, this is very similar to the original
ending that was cut from the first movie,

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.279
which Christopher Landon explained in the
Q&amp;A.

00:10:58.279 --> 00:10:59.279
Roll it

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:04.639
“The original ending of the movie that we
shot, Tree survives the fight and then wakes

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.529
up in a hospital and then the Doctor kind
of rushes everybody out because she needs

00:11:08.529 --> 00:11:13.360
a rest, and then this nurse comes in, and
starts to put something into Tree’s IV line,

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.540
and then she says, ‘oh no, no, you’re
not supposed to be doing that, and the nurse

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:22.180
pulls her mask down and reveals that it’s
Gregory’s wife, and she’s basically like

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.180
**** you.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.940
And then she kills her.”

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.541
So it’s interesting to see that ending kind
of found a home in the sequel.

00:11:29.541 --> 00:11:33.070
But there are some issues with the ending,
and when you’re dealing with time travel,

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:34.540
these things tend to come up.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.420
At the very beginning Ryan passes by the trumpet
player in the hall, which as I mentioned,

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.160
is heard every morning on the 18th.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:45.079
However, when Ryan gets to dorm room, he sees
this unfold, which is Tuesday the 19th, which

00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.850
is after Tree killed Lori and got out of the
time loop.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:51.390
I went back to the first Happy Death Day to
see if the trumpet is also played on the morning

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.380
of the 19th, and it is not.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.180
“Oh hey, you’re up”.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:03.940
Also, the whole thing with Ryan encountering
another version of himself isn’t consistent

00:12:03.949 --> 00:12:06.250
with anything that happens for the rest of
the movie.

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:10.889
For example, when Tree is sent to Dimension
B, she never encounters Tree B and the nerds

00:12:10.889 --> 00:12:14.590
tell her that the event likely caused Tree
B to be sent to another dimension altogether.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:18.860
I also didn’t really get what the point
was of introducing a second Ryan, or having

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.240
Ryan A go through the time loop at all at
the beginning of the movie, because when Tree

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.550
returns to dimension A at the end, it never
shows them solving the second time loop, unless

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:31.430
the math that the nerds from Dimension B used
somehow solved all time loops in all dimensions,

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.430
but that wouldn’t make sense because then
some other Bayfield Students in some far superior

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:39.519
dimension could have just solved everything
without Tree A ever having to do anything.

00:12:39.519 --> 00:12:43.330
So by all logical means, when Tree A gets
back to Dimension A, they should still have

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:47.820
to solve the issue of Ryan continually resetting
Tuesday the 19th, unless he’s saving that

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:48.830
for the third movie.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:52.040
But that doesn’t seem to be the case because
the mid-credits sequence suggests that the

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:56.899
next movie will revolve around Danielle being
tested as a time loop experiment by the DARPA

00:12:56.899 --> 00:13:00.420
agent Isaac Parker, which in itself doesn’t
make any sense because they would run into

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:03.949
the same problem that the Bayfield nerds had
in trying to figure out the correct algorithm

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:07.730
to close the time loops, an issue they were
only able to solve because Tree had the Reading

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:11.829
Steiner ability and she was somehow able to
remember every single equation that they tested

00:13:11.829 --> 00:13:15.640
-- which, by the way presents a problem of
it’s own because Tree’s body started to

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.070
deteriorate in the first Happy Death Day and
she only dies 11 times in that.

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:22.839
In Happy Death Day 2U, it shows her killing
herself about five times I think it was, we’ll

00:13:22.839 --> 00:13:26.079
have to ask Dead Meat, but she’d also have
to have way more off-screen deaths in order

00:13:26.079 --> 00:13:29.639
to afford her the time to memorize all of
those equations… unless of course she just

00:13:29.639 --> 00:13:33.420
has a photographic memory that conveniently
doesn’t work when she gets too drunk.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:37.570
Now to be fair, she did do a similar thing
in the first movie when she was able to recall

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:41.410
everyone on her suspects list every day, but
that’s still considerably less information

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:42.880
than the equations.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.000
But anyways, back to Danielle.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:49.460
The DARPA agent was going to use her as a test subject,
but they would have no way of tracking the

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:54.160
progress of their experiments unless Danielle
remembers everything from each day, and relays

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:58.350
them the information each time she comes though,
something I have a hard time believing she

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:00.980
would ever agree to or be capable of.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:04.839
But all of that aside, there just seem to
be some inconsistencies with Dimension B.

00:14:04.839 --> 00:14:08.759
Like for example, there is one morning where
Tree wakes up and doesn’t interrupt Carter

00:14:08.759 --> 00:14:13.009
B, and he goes on to ask her if she remembers
his name like the does in the first one…

00:14:13.009 --> 00:14:16.519
but wait they should already kind of know
each other in Dimension B. He’s dating Danielle,

00:14:16.519 --> 00:14:20.720
who is best friends with Tree in this dimension
and when Danielle comes up to the table she

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:25.290
acts like it’s completely normal for Carter,
Tree, Ryan, Samir and Anna to be hanging out.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:29.210
Then there’s the fact that the last play-through
of Dimension B ends with Dean Bronson and

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:32.959
the two security guys coming to confiscate
the Sissy machine one day early, and while

00:14:32.959 --> 00:14:35.759
that could be explained by the fact that he
might have just noticed the lights on the

00:14:35.759 --> 00:14:39.470
fritz again and decided to put and end to
it, he specifically says that he told them

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:43.860
not to power it on again, which he never did
in Dimension B, because Tree never reached

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.020
Tuesday the 19th in that dimension.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:51.130
But the real question we need to figure out…
the thing that could make or break all of

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:56.899
what I just said is… does anyone actually even care
besides me?

00:14:56.899 --> 00:14:58.800
"Back to the lab again."

